CONTENT
-------

This distribution includes the source of YicesTRA, tests, and examples.
YicesTRA is built on top of Yices 2, whose source, documentation and
binaries are included as well. The file README.md explains how to use
YicesTRA.


PREREQUISITES
-------------

To build YicesTRA from the source, you need:

- GCC version 4.9.x or newer (or clang 3.3 or newer)
- GNU make, and other standard tools (sed, etc.)
- gperf version 3.0 or newer
- the GMP library version 4.1 or newer
- SRI's library for polynomial manipulation, libpoly
  (https://github.com/SRI-CSL/libpoly)
- the CUDD library for binary-decision diagrams. We recommend the
  github distribution (https://github.com/ivmai/cudd), configured with
  option --enable-shared
- the FLINT library, version 3 or newer, which includes the Arb module
  (https://flintlib.org)
- the MPFR library (https://www.mpfr.org)


QUICK INSTALLATION
------------------

In the toplevel directory, do this:

  autoconf
  ./configure
  make

The binary of YicesTRA is then build/<platform>-release/bin/ytra, for
instance build/x86_64-pc-linux-gnu-release/bin/ytra on Linux.

You may need to provide CPPFLAGS and LDFLAGS if ./configure fails to
find a library. Other options may be useful too: try ./configure --help
to see what's there. README.md lists solutions to common problems.

To install ytra in /usr/local/bin/, then do:

  sudo make install

Only ytra is installed: the other binaries and the library of Yices 2
remain in the build directory. You can change the installation location
by giving option --prefix=... to the ./configure script.


OTHER PLATFORMS
---------------

The instructions above are for Unix systems. For the other platforms
supported by Yices 2, see doc/COMPILING, which explains the
compilation process of Yices 2 in detail.


DOCUMENTATION
-------------

The ./doc directory contains the documentation of Yices 2:

- doc/COMPILING explains the compilation process and options in detail.
- doc/NOTES gives an overview of the source code.
- doc/YICES-LANGUAGE explains the syntax of the Yices language, and
  describes commands, functions, and heuristic parameters.

To build the manual of Yices 2 (./doc/manual/manual.pdf), which needs a
latex installation and the latexmk tool, type

   make doc
